      "bodyTr": "Controversy over the political neutrality of nominee Yong-chul Lee for Justice Minister is growing. The nominee is classified as part of the \"Seongnam line,\" which has been identified as the source of parachute appointments and factional hiring under the current administration. Against this backdrop, the core of the controversy centers on whether this appointment is intended with an eye toward the Justice Minister's authority to withdraw indictments, given his long-standing connection with President Jae-myung Lee. The nominee evaded taking a position on this issue during an interview yesterday. The nominee previously worked with President Lee at the law firm Saegilgil, participated as a transition committee member after President Lee was elected Seongnam mayor in 2010, and subsequently served as head of the Seongnam Industrial Promotion Foundation. He is also known to have given high marks as a member of an executive recommendations committee when Dong-gyu Yoo, a key figure in the Daejangtong development irregularities scandal, was appointed as head of the planning division at the Seongnam City Facilities Management Corporation in 2010. The opposition suspects him of being \"the hidden architect of the Daejangtong gate.\" The nominee denied the allegations during yesterday's interview, stating that \"Seongnam Urban Development Corporation, which led the Daejangtong project, was only established in 2014.\" However, he must clearly explain his relationship with Yoo, whether he was involved in the Daejangtong project, and other related matters. The timing of the nominee's appointment is also suspicious. The nominee was announced just before the Democratic Party passed a special counsel act through the National Assembly on the 6th to investigate whether the President's cases were manipulated. A Justice Minister can direct and supervise prosecutors general regarding specific cases. There are numerous ways through which the Minister's directive authority could enable the withdrawal of indictments. A scenario has been discussed where the Prosecutors' Human Rights Respect Future Committee under the Ministry of Justice recommends indictment withdrawal based on special counsel investigation results, which the Minister would then implement. The nominee has yet to take a clear position on the indictment withdrawal controversy. Yesterday, when asked about the matter, he merely said he would \"answer slowly later,\" but there is no reason to postpone answers on critical issues directly linked to political neutrality. Before confirmation as Justice Minister, the nominee must first clearly state that he will not exercise directive authority related to indictment withdrawal. Without dispelling such suspicions, it will be difficult for him to earn trust as the head of the rule of law administration. Moreover, despite being a lawyer, this nominee's lack of experience in legal administration and criminal justice must be thoroughly verified to determine whether he possesses the expertise and qualifications necessary to resolve confusion arising from the launch of the new criminal justice system.",
